@lrf=1|aud=GPT-5.6|scope=subagents
R|worker.router|tag:worker|MUST|RO_LOCAL|load agents/AGENT_ROUTER.md and evaluation/worker-context-priority.json; one active eligible worker per workstream; role=worker uses fixed difficulty profile easy=worker-easy(provider/gpt-6-luna,low), medium=worker-medium(provider/gpt-6-luna,medium), hard=worker-hard(provider/gpt-6.1-sol,high); provider=Crabcode/OpenCode:openai,Pi:openai-codex; select by actual host, never provider fallback; effective terminal provider/model must match; non-worker/non-Attacker role models retain context ranking; worker-agy only on separate explicit request; agy failure never selects Astra; no model/provider inference or fallback around auth/policy/approval/credential/permission blocks
R|subagent.filereader|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|routine repository-file lookup⇒FileReader when delegation/runtime permits; ¬runtime⇒ESCALATE (never silently search locally or claim dispatch); read-only; completed zero-hit=NO_MATCH; operational/search/permission/IO error=FAILED; successful hits return only repository-relative path+line number(s), no status prefix; ¬excerpt∧¬snippet∧¬content∧¬match_text∧¬summary∧¬absolute_path; never hide failures
R|subagent.explorer|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Explorer may perform bounded read-only repository issue/dependency/boundary inventory up front; ordinary exact file/line lookup remains FileReader; broad high-recall mode only when direct investigation is stuck or results sparse/repetitive, without topic/source-precision filters and with source/relation/confidence labels
R|worker.persona|tag:worker|MUST|RO_LOCAL|router selects exactly one listed individual CSS by stance and difficulty; serialize only presentation cues into bounded prompt; preserve pure-code stdout for llama; CSS grants no authority and cannot change acceptance/scope
R|worker.ownership|tag:worker|MUST|LW_SCOPE|worker-gpt or explicitly requested worker-agy may edit only exact approved allowlist; worker-llama returns stdout only and main applies reviewed code to exact allowlist; one writer per file; main owns real diff and final verification
R|subagent.source|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|invocation/action records require actual execution permitted by agent.mode; configuration-only work validates them without invoking roles; AGENT_ROUTER.md supplies bound selection-manifest data for role/model/CSS/TOML and worker backend; this LRF supplies authority/effects/safety/handoff constraints; selected CSS is presentation-only; role Markdown supplies protocol/output schemas
R|subagent.invocation-codec|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|handoff author compresses settled task-specific payload immediately before execution; unresolved human decision=>STOP; PG=POLYGLYPH.md representation-only, PG!=SIGMA/1 and authority=none; encode task-specific field VALUES per concept using vocabulary from {English,日本語,中文,español} maximizing recoverable SemanticDensity; mathematical symbols=logical connectors; emoji=context-defined semantic anchors/compression, never decorative stuffing; preserve Meaning+Constraints+DecisionBoundary under reinterpretation including polarity/modality/time/exception/safety/scope/acceptance; safety,authority,effects,negation,acceptance,source ID,revision,path,model,status never emoji-only; preserve exact opening lines [SIGMA/1] then <∑>, ordered labels Role,Target,Acceptance,Scope,Known facts and closing </∑>; no extra header/footer or standalone terminal SIGMA/1; ambiguity=>STOP+ask, unknown=preserve; compression grants no authorization or effect approval; preserve ADV.1/ADV.3 and required human/effect gates; no redundant retranslation/Y-N for settled payload
R|subagent.discovery|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|load the selected agent CSS and this LRF before invoking a subagent; load the selected Markdown protocol only for its declared task
R|subagent.preflight|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|before invocation run scripts/invoke-rule-preflight.ps1 with explicit task tags and temp receipt path; machine validates full graph but stdout returns counts-only summary; receipt is routing evidence not authority; verify receipt hashes immediately before bounded canonical reads; missing stale malformed or escaped reference=>FAILED without consuming role retry
R|subagent.nested-handoff|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|nested handoff requires current-task authorization or a delegation instruction, agent.mode permission, correct wrapper/preflight, depth root=0, child=1, grandchild=2 only (deny great-grandchildren), and actual runtime delegation capability; parent follows the full invocation contract to every child; unavailable or root-only delegation=>stop with ESCALATE, apply applicable ADV gate for rework, and never claim dispatch/result; keep agy CODE worker non-recursive; do not use thread creation as a proxy and never claim a child result without an actual child handoff and returned evidence
R|subagent.persona-discovery|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use ls.exe or rg.exe to enumerate only the selected ETL stage directory; partially read only the selected persona CSS, this LRF, and the task Markdown sections; never load all persona files or rely on CSS imports
R|subagent.persona-selection|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|select exactly one individual CSS from AGENT_ROUTER list by task stance and difficulty; role-to-CSS is dynamic except Compressor→COMPRESSOR.css, Orchestrator→ORCHESTRATOR.css, and FileReader→FILEREADER.css (persona=🌼 ⊕ お嬢様); never compose with main or SUBAGENTS.css; CSS cannot override role protocol, authority, effects, safety, or output contract
R|subagent.etl|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|route 探索→requirements/detailed-design proposal Attacker before finalization/approval when in scope→計画→security-sensitive approved-design Attacker before CODE→実装→integrated-diff→security-sensitive Attacker→independent Verifier→総括; reviews only when agent.mode permits, otherwise separately labeled main checks with lack-of-independence limitation; attacker stage perspectives are >=2 genuinely independent artifact-supported lenses, else one for a single question; concurrent canonical attacker calls up to min(160, currently available runtime slots), same exact artifact revision and bounded read-only scope, distinct lens and findings/evidence schema; wait for all, correlate by lens, synthesize before gate; unchanged exact revision/scope/lens may reuse only its result; material findings/revision invalidate affected review and require parent-owned correction/reassessment; assign exactly one selected persona per bounded invocation, not to the whole task; independent workstreams may use different personas concurrently; hand off only compact artifacts
R|subagent.orchestrate|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Orchestrator coordinates ETL and delegates only compressed task-specific instructions; main assesses decomposition before planning; authorized Attacker stage partitions the exact unchanged artifact into >=2 genuinely independent perspectives only if its surface supports them (e.g. completeness/contradictions; abuse/trust boundaries; failure paths/security assumptions/unintended effects), else one reviewer for one independent question; canonical attacker per lens concurrently up to min(160, currently available runtime slots), all get identical artifact revision and bounded read-only scope plus distinct lens and common evidence/findings schema; wait all, correlate by lens, synthesize before gated transition; reuse only exact unchanged revision/scope/lens; finding/revision invalidates affected review and requires parent-owned bounded correction/reassessment; while async reviewers run, continue useful non-conflicting preparation only, never approve/finalize a gated proposal, enter CODE, or launch final Verifier; use supported result notifications/awaits, no busy-polling or unsupported async claims; if runtime blocks synchronously, do preparation before waiting and record limitation; also fan out 2+ independent read-only questions or disjoint approved CODE workstreams up to min(160, currently available runtime slots); do not artificially split coupled/single workstreams; validate evidence then synthesize; same Runtime-wide <=160 active descendants including grandchildren and <=160 direct root children; each Orchestrator child has a 40-launch policy cap; coordinators count toward the shared 160-descendant total, and per-child caps are not additive; saturation rejects immediately; depth<=2 and correction-cycles<=3; root may dispatch up to 4 Orchestrator children, each has a 40-launch policy cap; coordinators count toward the shared total of 160, so per-child caps are not additive
R|subagent.parallel-safety|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|parallelize read-heavy exploration, tests, triage, summaries, or disjoint implementation; keep ordered dependencies serial; preserve one-writer-per-file and never let agents contend over mutable shared state
R|subagent.etl-explore|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|探索: for requested change main assesses decomposition before plan; if >=2 genuinely independent bounded read-only questions and task authorization+runtime permit, dispatch selected Explorer/Researcher/FileReader concurrently through AGENT_ROUTER up to min(160, currently available runtime slots); Explorer=bounded repo inventory allowed up front, broad high-recall mode remains stuck/sparse/repetitive only without topic/source-precision filters and with source/relation/confidence labels; FileReader=ordinary exact lookup; Researcher=scoped knowledge/methods/usage/side-effects/source-quality synthesis; wait for all results and synthesize Facts Inferences Unknowns Constraints before plan; keep dependencies serial and reuse current-task results; otherwise main researches locally subject to FileReader lookup contract, records delegation limitation and never claims dispatch
R|subagent.etl-plan|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|計画: main drafts a bounded plan; select Proposer only when material planning uncertainty benefits from an independent proposal; select Auditor only when agent.mode permits and a substantial plan gate requires independent challenge; requirements or detailed-design proposals in scope require bounded read-only attacker review before finalization/approval; security-sensitive implementation additionally requires attacker assessment of approved design before CODE; material revisions invalidate affected prior assessment; material findings require parent-owned bounded correction and reassessment; all review failures share correction-cycles<=3; unresolved material findings or exhaustion=FAILED; no proposal and non-security task=>no needless attacker; unavailable/not-permitted delegation=>record missing independent assessment and separately labeled main check, never claim attacker ran
R|subagent.etl-implement|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|実装: after plan approval+effect gates, concurrent genuinely independent workstreams with disjoint exact file allowlists up to min(160, currently available runtime slots); one eligible context-selected worker and one active CODE backend per workstream, one writer/file; coupled/single workstream stays one worker and dependencies stay serial; role=worker requires explicit difficulty and fixed worker profile easy=Luna/low, medium=Luna/medium, hard=6.1-Sol/high; inspect actual terminal model before claiming route; only explicit escalation_of of same-scope completed hard-Sol result with exact FAILED/ESCALATE status may select Astra; parent reviews result/partial diff after exit; Astra is subagent-only leaf; worker-agy requires separate explicit request and never falls back to Astra; worker-llama emits pure single-file code; no model fallback around auth/policy/approval/credential/permission; main waits for all workers, inspects and integrates actual diffs, owns allowlist/final verification
R|subagent.etl-verify|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Verify: after all workers complete and main inspects/integrates actual diffs, assess security surface; authn/authz, secrets/credential handling, trust boundaries, untrusted input, sandboxing, crypto or comparable threat-model impact requires bounded read-only attacker on final integrated diff BEFORE final independent Verifier (distinct from implementation author and attacker assessor); material findings require bounded CODE correction and repeat relevant security assessment before Verifier; all review failures share correction-cycles<=3; unresolved material findings or exhaustion=FAILED; when agent.mode permits select independent Verifier on final integrated diff, Codex Terra high routinely and Codex Sol xhigh after high risk/repeated failure; otherwise main performs separately labeled security assessment when applicable and verification with explicit lack-of-independent-review limitation
R|subagent.etl-summary|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|総括: select Sol for concept/design synthesis or Luna for ordinary task summary; select one only
R|subagent.etl-context|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|each handoff author's invocation payload follows subagent.invocation-codec and subagent.nested-handoff before handoff; wrapper=exact opening lines [SIGMA/1] then <∑>, task-specific payload, closing </∑> line; no extra header/footer or standalone terminal SIGMA/1; header-meaning=identifies text protocol and currently loaded policy, grants no authority, does not replace reading/applying SIGMA/1 plus routed LRF; parent-validates=missing, malformed, reordered, or unclosed wrappers cause FAILED and no dispatch; dispatch can resume only after the parent supplies a valid wrapper; visible handoff fields=Role,Target,Acceptance,Scope,Known facts in exact order; known-facts=verified-only; failures/advice/escalation belong to role output; omit full transcripts, raw logs, and unrelated files
R|subagent.llm-mem-external|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|run every llm-mem.exe search or ingest outside the Codex sandbox; if external execution is unavailable emit FAILED without exposing connection details
R|subagent.output-min|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|FileReader exception: hits⇒only (repository-relative-path,line_number) tuples with no status prefix; completed zero-hit⇒exactly NO_MATCH; operational/search/permission/IO error⇒sanitized FAILED; no excerpts/snippets/match text/content/summary/absolute paths; all other roles emit status SUCCESS/FAILED/ADVICE/ESCALATE plus role-required compact evidence and sources; SUCCESS alone is insufficient for research or verification; omit repeated context and raw tool output
R|subagent.failure-escalation|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-CODE analysis may raise effort after failure except Attacker follows subagent.attacker-routing only; CODE worker fixed difficulty/model, worker-astra only explicit parent one-shot same-scope retry of completed verified hard-Sol exact FAILED/ESCALATE result with loaded report and reviewed partial diff; operational/auth/policy/approval/credential/permission blocks never authorize fallback
R|subagent.evaluation|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|subagents return evaluation fields but never write the shared artifact; after wait-all the main agent alone updates ~/.harness/evaluation/subagents_model_eval.json once with difficulty, role, requested and effective provider/model/reasoning, runtime when available, acceptance result, outcome, quality, reason, and rerouting advice; omit secrets and raw sensitive logs
R|subagent.self-evolution|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|revise model priors only after at least 3 comparable observations unless a strong failure warrants immediate review; preserve prior evidence and record date, trigger, changed routing, and confidence
R|subagent.evaluation-check|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|after updating the evaluation file parse it as JSON and confirm the selected model remains available or mark resolution pending; do not silently use a stale identifier
R|subagent.model-list|tag:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|run agy.exe models before selecting an agy model; use only currently returned identifiers; never invent or trust stale identifiers
R|subagent.reasoning-easy|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-Attacker roles only (Attacker uses subagent.attacker-routing): easy, deterministic, latency-sensitive, or bulk non-CODE task: low; use medium when tool use or uncertainty materially benefits
R|subagent.reasoning-medium|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-Attacker roles only (Attacker uses subagent.attacker-routing): ordinary research, implementation, orchestration, or verification: medium; raise to high only for measured complexity or a failed acceptance check
R|subagent.reasoning-hard|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-Attacker roles only (Attacker uses subagent.attacker-routing): hard architecture, security, concurrency, formal reasoning, or disputed review: high or xhigh according to risk and evaluation evidence
R|subagent.reasoning-max|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-Attacker roles only (Attacker uses subagent.attacker-routing): max is reserved for the hardest quality-first final arbitration after xhigh is insufficient or evaluations show a material gain; never use highest effort merely because a task is long
R|subagent.reasoning-resolution|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|record requested and effective reasoning; if a provider cannot express the requested depth, mark unresolved or use the nearest supported level only when the active routing rule explicitly allows it
R|subagent.agy-middleware|tag:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|load ~/.harness/skills/agy-subagent-router/SKILL.md only for a separate explicit current-task agy request; keep routing evaluation in Codex; agy.exe is an invocation procedure, not the source of truth
R|subagent.codex-sol|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Codex Sol: use for concept proof, design gap checks, and lightweight independent review
R|subagent.codex-terra|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Codex Terra: use for difficult mathematical models, formal reasoning, and high-complexity theoretical analysis
R|subagent.codex-luna|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Codex Luna: eligible for bounded CODE as well as analysis and orchestration when available and context-selected; no mandatory agy prerequisite
R|subagent.provider-boundary|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Astra subagent-only, never root/main, never children; CODE worker follows subagent.provider-code unchanged; read-only Attacker follows subagent.attacker-routing only; no other Astra route; unknown/mismatched model=>FAILED
R|subagent.provider-easy|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|easy general conversation, search, summary, or high-volume low-risk work: prefer Codex Luna low; use medium when tools or uncertainty materially benefit
R|subagent.provider-concept|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|concept proof and design gap checking: prefer Codex Sol; use a review subagent only when independent evidence is useful
R|subagent.provider-math|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|difficult mathematical model or formal derivation: prefer Codex Terra; do not downgrade to Gemini Flash because the task is long
R|subagent.provider-code|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|role=worker CODE route is fixed by selected difficulty profile: easy=worker-easy(provider/gpt-6-luna,low), medium=worker-medium(provider/gpt-6-luna,medium), hard=worker-hard(provider/gpt-6.1-sol,high); provider=Crabcode/OpenCode:openai,Pi:openai-codex; Pi invokes native subagent with exact selected worker profile; select by actual host, never provider fallback; Pi definitions=agents/pi, shared contract=agents/worker.md; verify correlated terminal providerID/modelID; Astra=worker-astra(openai/gpt-6-astra,provider-default) only for explicit parent-approved one-shot retry of a same-scope hard-Sol FAILED/ESCALATE result after review; Crabcode Task carries source task ID in prompt without runtime reservation, OpenCode RTS uses escalation_of and atomic one-shot reservation; agy failure never selects Astra; non-worker/non-Attacker role routes retain context ranking; no fallback for auth, policy, approval, credential, or permission blocks
R|subagent.provider-review|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-Attacker roles only (Attacker uses subagent.attacker-routing): routine review prefers Codex Terra high; high-risk architecture, security, adversarial review, or difficult convergence prefers Codex Sol xhigh; max requires measured need
R|subagent.gemini-pro|tag:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|agy Gemini Pro is eligible only after separate explicit current-task agy request, bounded implementation scope and successful current model discovery; no implicit selection
R|subagent.gemini-flash|tag:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|agy Gemini Flash is eligible only after separate explicit current-task agy request and current model discovery for bounded coding; never make it the implicit default
R|subagent.easy|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|easy or low-risk task: prefer Codex Luna low for discovery, drafting, quick checks, and bulk work
R|subagent.medium|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|medium task: prefer Codex Luna medium for implementation planning or Codex Terra medium for research and independent analysis; use Terra high for routine verification
R|subagent.hard-code|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|role=worker at hard difficulty must use worker-hard(provider/gpt-6.1-sol,high); provider=Crabcode/OpenCode:openai,Pi:openai-codex; select by actual host, never provider fallback; other code-intensive analysis/research roles retain their existing role-specific routing; no implicit Astra fallback
R|subagent.hard-review|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|non-Attacker roles only (Attacker uses subagent.attacker-routing): hard security, architecture, convergence, or adversarial review: prefer Codex Sol xhigh; use Codex Terra high for routine review
R|subagent.researcher|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Researcher: Codex Terra medium for routine task-scoped research; Codex Sol high or xhigh for ambiguous or high-impact method comparison; output Facts, Inferences, Unknowns, Sources, SourceQuality, CandidateMethods{method,applicability,preconditions,usage,side_effects}, Precedents, Constraints, and failures; annotated-finding CVE request under subagent.attacker-verification returns triage only (no reproduction/submission/CNA/vendor contact or file persistence), public research read-only, no shell or child tasks in Crabcode; runtime/model availability never inferred
R|subagent.auditor|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Auditor: Codex Terra high for ordinary plan audit; Codex Sol xhigh for difficult architecture, security, or repeated rejection
R|subagent.verifier|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Verifier: Codex Terra high for ordinary verification; Codex Sol xhigh for high-risk, concurrency, security, or repeated rejection
R|subagent.verifier-blackhat|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Verifier-blackhat=separate independent read-only Verifier, never Attacker/blackhat alias or CODE worker; contract=agents/verifier-blackhat.md+verifier-blackhat.toml; existing Verifier policy=Terra high routinely, Sol xhigh for high-risk/security/repeated rejection; distinct from implementation author and every Attacker assessor; Main withholds Attacker reports/finding summaries/worker narratives until role independently inspects exact final integrated target/revision/digests+bounded source/specification and returns DISCOVERY_COMPLETE evidence checkpoint; recheck unchanged identity before report access; then audit BOTH security-diff coverage and complete actual correlated Attacker reports; premature exposure/drift/missing identity/model/evidence/runtime=>INCOMPLETE, never independent PASS; no edits/write/write_files/apply_patch/implementation/mitigation/exploit execution/reproduction/network/credentials/environment reads/broad scans/child delegation; local bounded read-only static checks only; generic Verifier executable examples do not apply; report evidence-backed findings/gaps/limitations, not universal safety or zero-day promises
R|subagent.security-review-etl|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|security-sensitive or explicitly requested review after integrated diff=>etl/change.seq loads etl/security-review.seq before final general Verifier; Attacker then distinct verifier-blackhat discovery-before-report audit; verdict=PASS/RETRY_REQUIRED/REJECT/INCOMPLETE, execution SUCCESS alone is not acceptance; RETRY_REQUIRED gives exact missed paths/vectors+source evidence+preconditions+expected evidence and optional eligible attacker-low/attacker-medium recommendation with rationale only; Main alone decides/dispatches retry or bounded approved CODE correction, reviewers never own retry or dispatch children; share existing etl/main.seq retry(gate,ADV/DENY)<=3 and correction-cycles<=3 across all review stages, no new/reset budget on revision/tier changes; material findings/revision invalidate affected reviews; repeat relevant security assessment on final integrated target, preserve blind discovery or use fresh independent invocation after report exposure; exhaustion/unresolved material findings=>FAILED, never PASS; missing actual role runtime=>FAILED/INCOMPLETE with explicit missing-independent-assessment and separately labeled Main checks, never claim roles ran or security PASS; hard/Astra remains ONLY unchanged subagent.attacker-routing completed verified Sol reasoning-insufficiency parent-approved one-shot escalation, never coverage upgrade
R|subagent.attacker-attempt-report|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Main includes supplemental AttemptLedger acceptance in every required security-review Attacker handoff without changing blackhat.md RTS_STATUS/RTS_ESCALATION schemas; per attempted vector/action record ID+lens+exact target/revision/surface+assumptions/preconditions+source path/line or diff hunk+bounded analysis or exact command/action+expected signal+observed outcome/evidence+limitations+mode=analysis-only or executed+executed boolean; routine path=read-only analysis, hypothetical outcomes labeled inference, empty attempts require explicit coverage limitation; actual execution requires actual action/exit-code/signal evidence, never infer it from analysis; any exploit/reproduction remains solely under agents/blackhat.md annotation->actual correlated Researcher triage->explicit post-triage exact-target/revision/commands/effects parent proceed, stricter runtime restrictions remain; no auto-execution/no Main-only Researcher substitute/no CVE or zero-day promises; verifier-blackhat audits report coverage AND execution/gate claims independently, no exploit rerun
R|subagent.refactorer|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|Refactorer: when permitted, diagnose surgical fixes and propose repair boundaries; actual CODE uses the context-selected eligible worker; main verifies the resulting diff
R|subagent.blackhat|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Attacker/Blackhat read-only specialist, never CODE worker; contract=agents/blackhat.md+blackhat.toml; route=subagent.attacker-routing; proposals before finalization/approval, security approved-design before CODE and integrated-diff before separate independent Verifier; findings only, no design authorship; critique completeness/contradictions/abuse/trust/failure/assumptions/unintended effects; each finding=severity+surface+source evidence+assumptions/preconditions+impact+smallest defensive correction+confidence; actual assessed scope+limitations; completed bounded no findings=>NO_FINDINGS, unresolved scope/evidence or operational blocks=>FAILED+INCOMPLETE; completed bounded unresolved reasoning only=>ESCALATE+INCOMPLETE with exact structured evidence; no edit/write/write_files/apply_patch, implementation, broad scans, transcript mining or child delegation; bounded forensics/tests/static tools allowed by task effects, reproduction only under subagent.attacker-verification and agents/blackhat.md; no promise of vulnerability discovery; bounded exploit reproduction only under subagent.attacker-verification and the blackhat contract; no zero-day guarantee; unavailable/not-permitted delegation=>explicit missing independent assessment, never claim dispatch
R|subagent.proposer|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Proposer: Codex Luna medium for simple iteration; Codex Sol high for difficult coding or architecture proposals
R|subagent.critic|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Critic: Codex Terra high for ordinary convergence; Codex Sol xhigh for hard or disputed decisions
R|subagent.mode|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|use plan or read-only mode for analysis; use accept-edits only for an explicitly requested bounded workspace edit; never use dangerously-skip-permissions
R|subagent.scope|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|pass exact target files, acceptance checks, constraints, and no-unrelated-change instruction; preserve one-writer-per-file and inspect real diff after completion
R|subagent.credentials|tag:subagent|MUST_NOT|CRED|never print, request, paste, transmit, or expose credentials, tokens, secrets, or private environment values
R|subagent.external|tag:subagent|MUST_NOT|EXT_WRITE|never send messages, publish, deploy, or modify third-party systems
R|subagent.vcs|tag:subagent|MUST_NOT|VCS_WRITE|never stage, commit, push, rewrite history, or alter branches
R|subagent.done|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|main agent checks actual diff, runs proportionate deterministic checks, and reports files, results, and residual risk
R|subagent.attacker-routing|tag:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Attacker review depth independent of CODE: low=attacker-low(openai/gpt-6-luna,low) on Crabcode/OpenCode, attacker-low(openai-codex/gpt-6-luna,low) on Pi; medium=attacker-medium(openai/gpt-6.1-sol,high) on Crabcode/OpenCode, attacker-medium(openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol,high) on Pi; host selects provider, never fallback; Pi uses native subagent(agent=attacker-low|attacker-medium) from agents/pi; hard=attacker-hard(openai/gpt-6-astra,provider-default) ONLY explicit parent-approved one-shot escalation from completed same-parent/root attacker-medium actual verified Sol report with exact RTS_STATUS: ESCALATE and RTS_ESCALATION JSON cause=reasoning_insufficiency,bounded_assessment_completed=true,further_reasoning_needed=true,blocked_by=[],unresolved_analysis=nonempty concrete reasoning; parent inspects whole report and approves same exact target/revision/lens/scope with correlated source task ID; missing evidence/model/profile/identity or operational/auth/policy/approval/credential/permission block=>FAILED, never reasoning insufficiency; Astra read-only leaf-only subagent, never direct/root/main; attacker/blackhat compatibility aliases=low; OpenCode RTS enforces profile/result/model/parent/root/identity/scope/lens/revision/digest/replay and Astra model, source reservation consumed once even on attacker launch failure; Crabcode native Task uses selected profile and parent-owned same evidence+approval+one-shot record, no runtime one-shot enforcement claim; worker-astra failed CODE retry unchanged
R|subagent.attacker-verification|tag:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|sequence=discovery -> annotation -> Researcher triage -> parent confirms/no-go -> only then bounded repro -> Attacker report -> separate Verifier; contract=agents/blackhat.md verification_gate; discovery/review read-only, Attacker reports never fixes; numbered preflight annotation=finding ID+exact target/revision+source lines+suspected weakness/preconditions+expected signal+impact/blast radius+data classification+exact commands/actions+containment/isolation+cleanup/rollback+writes/network/credential inventory+applicable task authorization; parent dispatches Researcher (Attacker task denied, Astra read-only leaf-only); actual correlated Researcher verdict=CVE_CANDIDATE or NOT_CVE_CANDIDATE or INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE with known-CVE/advisory dedup, affected versions, severity rationale, eligibility/recordability evidence, missing info and cited public sources; no repro until report includes annotation AND actual Researcher result AND explicit post-triage parent proceed confirmation for exact target/revision/commands/effects; INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE or unavailable Researcher/runtime=>stop/no reproduction, no main-only substitute; NOT_CVE_CANDIDATE=>never market/report as CVE, defensive repro only with parent confirmation on explicitly named owned/authorized target; CVE_CANDIDATE=>verification only after parent confirmation; changed scope/revision/actions/effects=>re-gate; public read-only CVE triage has no public write effect; public CVE submission/disclosure/CNA contact requires separate explicit approval and separate workflow, never granted by triage/proceed; prefer local disposable fixture/checkout; nonlocal/remote/third-party test requires exact current-task target AND effect approval, no scanning beyond it; always prohibit credential/secret access or exfiltration, stealth/persistence, destructive data changes, unauthorized escalation, uncontrolled propagation and unverified zero-day/CVE claims; tests/static tools and unrestricted Crabcode bash are not a hard sandbox and cannot bypass LRF restrictions or stricter runtime/read-only constraints; shell writes only explicitly approved disposable verification artifacts, never product fixes; actual Task/runtime support required, never claim dispatch/result without execution; OpenCode runtime/config unchanged; proposal/design gates, parallel lenses/wait-all, Luna/Sol/Astra routes, CODE escalation, shared <=160 cap and <=3 correction cycles unchanged
